  "version": 1,
  "title": "The Golden Ratio as the Sharp Mahler Bound for Nonreciprocal Polynomials with Odd Coefficients",
  "abstract": "Every integer polynomial with all coefficients odd that differs from both signs of its reverse has multiplicative Mahler measure at least (1 + √5)/2. The polynomial x² − x − 1 meets all these hypotheses and attains the bound.",
